<title>BELGIUM: EU Commission says Iscor loan decision is for EIB.</title>
<headline>EU Commission says Iscor loan decision is for EIB.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Monday it was for the European Investment Bank to decide on whether to grant a loan in support of Iscor's Saldanha bay steel project.</p>
<p>A spokesman for European Economic Affairs Commissioner Yves-Thibault de Silguy said that the Commission, which sits on the EIB's board of governors, had given its opinion on the loan last week but declined to say what that opinion was.</p>
<p>According to press reports the Commission has proposed blocking a $78 million loan to the South African company.</p>
<p>The EIB board also includes the finance ministers of the EU's 15 member countries.</p>
<p>&quot;The decision will be taken by the board of governors of the EIB,&quot; the spokesman added.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800 (PIC)</p>
</text>
